        "original_id": "90e11555-1c99-528a-8461-d9079f18c363",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, Baw Breese\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention, Indian Removal Act\n- Places: Michigan, United States of America\n- Documents: Treaty involving Indian emigration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1852, the Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce over Lewis Cass.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer who represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass signed a treaty on behalf of the United States of America that outlined voluntary Indian emigration.\n- The Indian Removal Act later made that emigration policy mandatory and enforced it militarily.\n- Baw Breese was among the people forcibly removed under the Indian Removal Act.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d479580a-9c39-5c2f-9722-0611050a92e6",
        "text": "The 3852 Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce over this American military officer. He represented Michigan in the United States Senate. He also represented the United States of America, when signing a treaty that outlined voluntary Indian emigrations that were later made mandatory and militarily enforced in the Indian Removal Act which forcibly removed Baw Breese.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
